.el .ds Aq '
.TH dfdu-report 1  "dfdu-report " 
.SH NAME
dfdu\-report \- Scan a directory and list what the cleanup rules found in it: caches, build output, dependencies, with how safe each is to delete
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdfdu report\fR [\fB\-\-min\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-category\fR] [\fB\-\-older\-than\fR] [\fB\-\-safety\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-above\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-x\fR|\fB\-\-one\-file\-system\fR] [\fB\-\-cross\-mounts\fR] [\fB\-\-network\fR] [\fB\-\-mft\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan a directory and list what the cleanup rules found in it: caches, build output, dependencies, with how safe each is to delete
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-size\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Only matches at least this big (`100M`, `1.5GiB`, `500 KB`)
.TP
\fB\-\-category\fR \fI<CATEGORY>\fR
Only these categories (comma separated): an id such as `dev.build`, or its first part (`dev`) for all of them
.TP
\fB\-\-older\-than\fR \fI<AGE>\fR
Only matches unchanged for this long (`30d`, `2w`, `12h`; a bare number is days)
.TP
\fB\-\-safety\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
Only matches this safe or safer: safe, regenerable, review, manual or protected (all)
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-above\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Exit with code 4 when the matches listed, protected ones left out, add up to more than this (`5GiB`), for CI
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: table]
Output: table or json (schema/report.v1.json)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<THREADS>\fR
Worker threads
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-one\-file\-system\fR
Stay on the filesystem of the scanned directory (the default; overrides \-\-cross\-mounts and \-\-network given before it)
.TP
\fB\-\-cross\-mounts\fR
Descend into other local filesystems (disks, tmpfs)
.TP
\fB\-\-network\fR
Descend into network filesystems (NFS, SMB, sshfs and other FUSE network mounts); with or without \-\-cross\-mounts
.TP
\fB\-\-mft\fR
Windows, as administrator: read each NTFS volume\*(Aqs master file table instead of listing its directories, which is much faster on large volumes. Volumes whose table cannot be read are listed as usual
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

